Due to the surface waviness inherent to the DED-Arc process, specimens in the as-built condition do not exhibit a uniform nominal thickness. To account for this in the nominal stress calculation, the specimen thickness was determined using macroscopic cross-sections, following Method 2 described in [ 13 ]. For each specimen series, 6 cross-sections were prepared, binarized, and the local thickness was measured along a 27.5 mm segment at 0.13 mm intervals. The resulting data were statistically evaluated with respect to mean value and standard deviation. The effective nominal thickness was then calculated using Eq. ( 4 ) and used in combination with the respective specimen width to determine the nominal cross-sectional area. 4 t eff = t ¯ - 2 σ \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
